int lcs(String a, String b) {
    int m = a.length(), n = b.length();
    int[][] dp = new int[m + 1][n + 1];   // dp[0][*]=dp[*][0]=0 (base)
    for (int i = 1; i <= m; i++)
        for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {
            if (a.charAt(i-1) == b.charAt(j-1))
                dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + 1;          // match: diagonal +1
            else
                dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1]); // no match
        }
    return dp[m][n];
}

// a="AGGTAB", b="GXTXAYB" -> LCS "GTAB" length 4
```

```java
int knapsack(int[] wt, int[] val, int W) {
    int[] dp = new int[W + 1];
    for (int i = 0; i < wt.length; i++)
        for (int w = W; w >= wt[i]; w--)         // BACKWARD: each item once
            dp[w] = Math.max(dp[w], dp[w - wt[i]] + val[i]);
    return dp[W];
}

// wt={1,3,4,5}, val={1,4,5,7}, W=7
// best = items {weight3,weight4} -> value 4+5 = 9 -> dp[7]=9
```
Iterating `w` downward ensures `dp[w - wt[i]]` still refers to the **previous** item row.

